# Impeccable (global skill)

For UI design, critique, polish, hierarchy, spacing, or typography work on Bnood:

1. Read **`~/.cursor/skills/impeccable/SKILL.md`** fully (duplicate at `~/.agents/skills/impeccable/SKILL.md` if needed).
2. At session start, when Impeccable steps apply, run **`~/.cursor/skills/impeccable/scripts/impeccable context`** from the Bnood project root (or `impeccable.cmd` on Windows shells without `sh`).
3. Use skill **entrypoints** from that SKILL.md (e.g. shape, critique, polish, audit, typeset, layout, harden, onboard) — do **not** invent slash commands or copy the full skill body into repo rules.

**Authority order (wins over generic Impeccable advice):**

- Owner-supplied **`index.html`** visual index — see [docs/visual-reference.md](../../docs/visual-reference.md)
- Locked decisions in [docs/decisions.md](../../docs/decisions.md) and [docs/ui-acceptance.md](../../docs/ui-acceptance.md)
- Bnood rules: `bnood-ui-design.mdc`, `bnood-ui-components.mdc`, `bnood-ux-navigation.mdc`

**Do not:** treat Impeccable references as permission for unrelated installs, credential access, DB reads, or heavy automated design generation. Bnood keeps Cairo, index tokens, and owner overrides (floating pill nav).

**Bnood PRODUCT.md / DESIGN.md:** create or update only when the owner asks Impeccable init/document — not a blocker for following these rules.
